<title>FRANCE: Aero International wins Northwest plane order.</title>
<headline>Aero International wins Northwest plane order.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aero International, a venture of France's Aerospatiale, Italy's Alenia and British Aerospace, said Tuesday Northwest Airlines ordered 12 Avro RJ jets, with an option to acquire up to 24 more.</p>
<p>The order is valued at $300 million, Aero International said. It said the order brings the number of firm orders for the entire regional jet family to 105. So far, 72 RJs have been delivered worldwide.</p>
<p>Deliveries of the 69-seat jets will begin in April 1997 and proceed at a rate of around one a month.</p>
<p>The jets will be operated by Northwest's partner Mesaba Airlines on feeder routes from Northwest's hub airports in Minneapolis and Detroit.</p>
</text>
